Z||000000||GTMike||11-24-2001||12:39 PM||||well i changed my yesterday and put it all back together except for a few things.  and i got to thinking i didn't see  a spring in the bell housing to pull the throwout bearing back.  is there supose to be one??||||reg||1
Z||000001||Eriamjh||11-24-2001||12:50 PM||||I didn't see one when I did my 5-speed on my '87, so my answer is "no".<P>Any one else?||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-24-2001||12:58 PM||||In most hydraulic clutches... the throwout is kept in very light contact with the pressure plate. This makes the clutch self adjusting like a disk brake caliper.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||LZeitgeist||11-24-2001||12:59 PM||||Nope, no spring on the clutch arm.||||reg||1
Z||000004||The Aura||11-24-2001||12:59 PM||||Nope... not on my 86 GT 4spd.<P>------------------<BR>1986 GT 4spd&gt; Suspension Techniques Springs, Poly Bushings, Bosal Brospeed 4.5" Exhaust Tips, Cross Drilled Rotors||||reg||1
Z||000005||Archie||11-24-2001||03:21 PM||||Nope on all Stick Shift Fieros<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||StuGood||11-24-2001||04:04 PM||||Well, I really hate to differ with you all...<P>So I won't  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  None of my manual trans. Fieros has a return spring on the lever itself.  That includes:  1988 Isuzu 5-speed, 1987 Getrag 5-speed, 1986 Muncie 4-speed.  The 1986 <B>had</B> a return spring on the clutch <B>pedal</B>, which I removed per Archie's recommendation (on his web site).<P>So far so good - no springs, but many happy returns  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">    ||||reg||12
